kconfig: tolerate components absent from the public release

bouffalo_sdk v2.3.38 sources components/bflb_gmf/Kconfig and
components/av_render/Kconfig unconditionally, but the public release does
not ship either component, so configuring any project fails with
"'components/bflb_gmf/Kconfig' not found". Use osource for them, as the
same file already does for zigbee ("ships out-of-tree in external
releases"). Neither component is used by the Arduino package.

Applies to components/Kconfig of bouffalo_sdk v2.3.38 (946f92a0).
Drop this patch when sources.json moves to a release that ships these
components or marks them optional.

--- a/components/Kconfig
+++ b/components/Kconfig
@@ -18,8 +18,8 @@ source "$BL_SDK_BASE/components/os/Kconfig"
 source "$BL_SDK_BASE/components/iperf/Kconfig"
 source "$BL_SDK_BASE/components/shell/Kconfig"
 source "$BL_SDK_BASE/components/soln_utils/Kconfig"
-source "$BL_SDK_BASE/components/bflb_gmf/Kconfig"
-source "$BL_SDK_BASE/components/av_render/Kconfig"
+osource "$BL_SDK_BASE/components/bflb_gmf/Kconfig"
+osource "$BL_SDK_BASE/components/av_render/Kconfig"
 source "$BL_SDK_BASE/components/usb/Kconfig"
 source "$BL_SDK_BASE/components/utils/Kconfig"
 source "$BL_SDK_BASE/components/wamr/Kconfig"
